---
description: Flavors, navigation, CI, logging, and design docs for money-moving work
alwaysApply: true
---

# Ship & observe (mandatory)

- Flavors: `dev` / `staging` / `prod`. Base URLs and keys come from flavor config, never hard-coded in features.
- Navigation: typed routes (e.g. `go_router`). No raw route strings in widgets.
- Before any money-moving feature: a short design doc (settlement, idempotency, failure, eligibility). Wait for approval if the path is regulated.
- Legal, fee, APY, and risk copy is not invented by the agent. Use placeholders and flag for human/compliance review.
- Structured logging + crash reporting. Breadcrumbs on money-moving submits. Never log balances, tokens, seeds, or PII.
- CI must run unit (and money-flow widget) tests on the feature branch. Do not commit if CI/tests fail.
- Say “I don’t know” or “I was wrong” and correct course when needed.
